%% Full procedure: build-guides/GUIDE-01-Authentication.md section 4,
%% build-guides/GUIDE-08-Tenant-Onboarding.md

sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as IT Administrator
    participant Console as bheka-console
    participant Gateway as bheka-gateway
    participant Agent as bheka-agent (new device)
    participant Vault as eride-vault

    Admin->>Console: Generate installer config for tenant
    Console->>Gateway: POST /v1/admin/tenants/{id}/installer-config
    Gateway-->>Console: Single-use enrolment token + installer package
    Admin->>Agent: Install MSI with TENANT_ID, ENROLMENT_TOKEN, SERVER_URL, TIER

    Agent->>Agent: Generate keypair, build CSR (rcgen)
    Agent->>Vault: EnrolAgent(csr, enrolment_token) over mTLS bootstrap channel
    Vault->>Vault: Validate token (single-use, not expired, matches tenant)
    Vault->>Vault: Sign certificate with issuing CA
    Vault-->>Agent: Signed agent certificate + tenant X25519 public key

    Agent->>Agent: Store certificate, store tenant public key (never private key)
    Agent->>Gateway: Heartbeat (bheka.agent.enrolled.v1 published)
    Gateway-->>Admin: Enrolment confirmed in console

    Note over Agent,Vault: From this point, all agent-Vault contact is<br/>renewal-only. Agent never requests decrypt capability.
